              "date": "2025-08-26T16:45",
              "body": "Discharge summary reviewed: admitted 8/14-8/21 with severe alcoholic hepatitis; peak bili 8.4, PT 18.4 (control 12.0), DF 38; cultures negative; prednisolone 40 mg daily from 8/15 for 28 days; Lille 0.31 at day 7.\n\nS: Here with wife. No alcohol since admission, 12 days. Taking prednisolone every morning, day 12. Sleeping poorly on it, appetite huge. Eyes still yellow but less. No confusion, no bleeding, no fever.\n\nMeds reconciled: as per discharge list, prednisolone stops after the 9/11 dose.\n\nO: Wt 79.0. Vitals in flowsheet. Jaundiced sclerae. Spider angiomas. Abdomen soft, mildly distended, no fluid wave. No asterixis. No edema.\n\nA/P:\n1. Severe alcoholic hepatitis on cirrhosis, responding to prednisolone - labs today. Finish course 9/11, no taper. GI visit 9/17 is booked.\n2. AUD - abstinent 12 days. Strong praise. Offered psychiatry/counseling again - he will think about it; wife will help.\n3. Infection precautions on steroids reviewed; call for fever.\n4. Others unchanged.\n\nRTC 6-8 weeks."
