              "body": "Outside Gastroenterology Clinic Note\nDate of service: 09/17/2025\n\nFollow-up after admission for severe alcoholic hepatitis (DF 38) treated with prednisolone 40 mg daily x 28 days, completed 9/11; Lille 0.31 at day 7.\n\nHe reports no alcohol since admission. Jaundice is fading. Appetite good. No confusion or bleeding.\n\nExam: mild scleral icterus. Abdomen soft, no fluid wave. No asterixis.\n\nImpression: alcoholic hepatitis improving after steroids, alcoholic cirrhosis.\n\nPlan: complete and lasting abstinence is the single most important factor for survival; reinforced with him and his wife. Labs every 4-8 weeks through primary care. GI follow-up in 6 months or sooner.\n\nGastroenterology"
