              "body": "GI note 9/17 reviewed: improving after steroids, labs q4-8 wk here, GI in 6 months.\n\nS: Two months without a drink. 'Hardest thing I've done.' Still smoking a pack a day; says one thing at a time. Weight up, eating well. Back at work full time.\n\nO: Wt 81.5. Vitals in flowsheet. Faint scleral icterus. Abdomen soft, nondistended. No edema.\n\nPHQ-9 5.\n\nA/P:\n1. Alcoholic hepatitis/cirrhosis - better; bili down. Labs today.\n2. AUD - in early remission, 2 months. Continue whatever is working; psychiatry door open.\n3. Tobacco - advised.\n4. Flu and COVID today.\n5. NSCLC - CT December.\n\nRTC January for physical."
