              "title": "Annual Physical",
              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2026-01-14T09:00",
              "body": "ANNUAL PHYSICAL\n\n55 y/o M. Interval: admitted 8/2025 for severe alcoholic hepatitis, prednisolone x 28 days; abstinent through the fall. CT 12/16 without recurrence of the RUL NSCLC.\n\nS: Started drinking again around the holidays - 'just beer' at first, now most days, and he admits some vodka. Feels he 'let everyone down.' Tired. Some bloating. No yellow eyes he has noticed. No bleeding, no confusion. Smoking a pack a day.\n\nMeds reviewed: albuterol prn, ipratropium QID, Creon 36,000 with meals and snacks, omeprazole 20, aspirin 81, atorvastatin 40, thiamine, folic acid, MVI. NKDA.\n\nExam: Wt 81.0. Vitals in flowsheet. Faint scleral icterus. No lymphadenopathy. Lungs prolonged expiration. Heart RRR. Abdomen soft, nondistended. Femoral pulses faint. Feet intact. No edema.\n\nAUDIT-C 10. PHQ-9 6.\n\nA/P:\n1. AUD relapse - discussed without judgment; the fall shows he can do it. Referral back to addiction psychiatry offered; he will call them. Acamprosate again offered; declined.\n2. Cirrhosis / alcoholic hepatitis - labs today. GI due in March.\n3. Health maintenance: FIT kit given. Lipids today. Vaccines current.\n4. NSCLC - next CT June.\n\nRTC 3 months, sooner if yellow or swelling."
            }
